{
  "claims": [
    "In the area of Canneto sull'Oglio, Casalmoro and Casalromano, the enrollment rate for telemonitoring among patients living alone at more than 40 km is 15.38%, involving 13 patients, significantly below the regional threshold of 60 points below (regional value: 87.01%).",
    "At the municipal level, the municipalities of Canneto sull'Oglio (63.64%) and Casalmorano (72. 73%) show telemonitoring enrollment rates below 75%, while Solferino (46.15%) is particularly critical, with a value below 50%.",
    "In the ASST Mantova, there are 73 patients with delayed telemonitoring, with a maximum delay of 98 days; the patients at highest risk are p_03980 (98 days) and p_03811 (97 days), with low risk scores (0.0596 and 0.0392).",
    "In the ASST Mantova, the compliance rate for the Heart Failure pathway is 66.67% for the telemonitoring phase, 73.68% for the echocardiogram, and 74.59% for the cardiology visit, indicating overall adherence below 75% across multiple steps."
  ],
  "conclusion": "The alarm is caused by very low telemonitoring adherence in specific municipalities of ASST Mantova (Canneto sull'Oglio, Casalmoro, Casalromano, Solferino), particularly among patients living alone at more than 40 km. Delayed telemonitoring is widespread (73 patients delayed), and ASST Mantova shows overall adherence below 75% across multiple steps. The intervention must focus on these municipalities, with particular emphasis on Solferino and Canneto sull'Oglio, and on patients with delays, to improve adherence and reduce the risk of hospitalization."
}
